            href="https://www.abundanceandgrowth.org/p/ordinary-abundance"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">the Abundance and Growth blog</a
          >. The Bellamy passage is dialogue from chapter 11 of
          <a
            href="https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/bellamy-ed/works/backward/ch11.htm"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>Looking Backward</em> (1888)</a
          >, where the endless music is delivered, fittingly, by wire from
          central halls. The Wabash, Croton water and Calcutta ice
          quotations are as the site presents them.
        </li>
        <li>
          Ester Strogen's lease was reported by
          <a
            href="https://www.nbcnews.com/id/wbna14838642"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">NBC News / AP in 2006</a
          > and revisited by
          <a
            href="https://www.computerworld.com/article/1522250/at-t-charges-elderly-widow-14-000-in-rent-for-rotary-phone.html"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Computerworld</a
          >; the figures are her family's estimates. The
          <a
            href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carterfone"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Carterfone decision</a
          > opened the Bell network to customer-owned equipment in 1968, and
          <a
            href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/QLT_Consumer_Lease_Services"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">QLT Consumer Lease Services</a
          > still had roughly 580,000 telephone-leasing customers in 2007.
        </li>
        <li>
          The rented pineapple of eighteenth-century Britain is covered by
          <a
            href="https://www.mentalfloss.com/article/65506/super-luxe-history-pineapples-and-why-they-used-cost-8000"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Mental Floss</a
          >. The iceman's rounds and their end at the hands of the electric
          refrigerator are described by the
          <a
            href="https://americanhistory.si.edu/explore/stories/keeping-your-food-cool-ice-harvesting-electric-refrigeration"
